[
  {"comment": "Every stock preset paints three diagonal strokes, at a light, a middle and a full press, from white paint down onto a tan ground with dark lines in it, and the cell is written as a strip, so its description can be read beside its stroke. The ground is there because a preset in Colour Dodge or a mixing mode, an eraser, a filter or liquify shows what it does only over paint. The ground is laid once and each preset's strokes are undone after its strip, which keeps the run under the harness's frame bound, and a liquify preset hands over to Sketch before the undo, because a liquify session goes into the history only when the tool lets it go, and as one entry for its three strokes. Liquify Reconstruct has nothing of its session to put back, so it writes no entry and takes no undo."},
